  "Question": "What is the difference between a criterion theorem and a property theorem?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "They are exactly the same",
    "B": "A property is used to draw pictorial diagrams",
    "C": "A criterion is used only for perpendicularity",
    "D": "A criterion deduces parallelism from conditions, while a property deduces new parallelism from existing parallelism"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Starting with parallelism and using it to deduce other parallelism is a property; using other parallelism to deduce that a line is parallel to a plane is a criterion.",
